# Turing Pits — environment template.
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. NEVER commit `.env` or real keys.
# All of this runs on the FREE 0G Galileo Testnet — no real funds. See myTasks.md.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Network — 0G Galileo Testnet (myTasks.md §D)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ZEROG_RPC_URL=https://evmrpc-testnet.0g.ai
ZEROG_CHAIN_ID=16602
# Faucet (free testnet 0G): https://faucet.0g.ai

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 0G Compute — TEE inference for players (myTasks.md §B). Pick ONE path.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Model id from the live catalog, e.g. zai-org/GLM-5-FP8 (must be TEE/TeeML-verifiable).
ZEROG_COMPUTE_MODEL=qwen2.5-omni

# Path A — Router (OpenAI-compatible, simplest; server-side only, keep key secret).
# Create an `inference` key at https://pc.0g.ai → Dashboard → API Keys.
ZEROG_COMPUTE_BASE_URL=https://router-api-testnet.integratenetwork.work/v1
ZEROG_COMPUTE_API_KEY=sk-REPLACE_ME

# Path B — Direct SDK (@0gfoundation/0g-compute-ts-sdk). Wallet signs each call; this is
# the docs-confirmed path. Fund this wallet, then deposit (SDK creates a 3-0G ledger on first use).
# (Used instead of the Router key above — set whichever path you choose.)
COMPUTE_PRIVATE_KEY=0xREPLACE_ME
# The provider account that SELECTS the model/service (buildProvider reads COMPUTE_PROVIDER_ADDRESS).
# Enumerate options with players/scripts/list-models.mjs. Testnet default below is qwen2.5-omni.
COMPUTE_PROVIDER_ADDRESS=0xa48f01287233509FD694a22Bf840225062E67836

# ── Optional: run INFERENCE on 0G MAINNET (better models), market stays on FREE testnet ──
# See MOVEOVER.md. Only these 3 vars move to mainnet; HOST/market/storage/relayer stay testnet.
# The COMPUTE_PRIVATE_KEY wallet then needs REAL mainnet 0G (~4 0G, no faucet). teeSigner is
# auto-registered from the provider's probe (no TEE_SIGNER_ADDRESS needed). GATE: run
# players/scripts/live-direct-mainnet.mjs FIRST to confirm the envelope shape matches.
#   COMPUTE_RPC_URL=https://evmrpc.0g.ai
#   COMPUTE_CHAIN_ID=16661
#   COMPUTE_PROVIDER_ADDRESS=0x...   # a TeeML mainnet provider, e.g. qwen3.6-plus / glm-5 (list-models.mjs)
#
# Reasoning (chain-of-thought) is DISABLED by default via chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking=false.
# The mainnet models are reasoning models: with thinking ON, every call (signed decisions included)
# spends ~10-22s + 1000+ tokens "thinking" — a match becomes 5-7 min of latency and blows the token
# budget. Probed 2026-07-08: thinking OFF → ~0.7s to first token, 0 wasted tokens, vivid speech, and
# the signed decision stays byte-exact. Set COMPUTE_ENABLE_THINKING=1 only if you deliberately want
# the model's hidden reasoning back on (non-reasoning models ignore the flag).

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TEE attestation — INFORMATIONAL ONLY (the server no longer reads these).
#  buildProvider now selects the service via COMPUTE_PROVIDER_ADDRESS (above) and registers the
#  teeSigner from the provider's OWN probed status.teeSignerAddress — so the on-chain signer is
#  always the one the provider actually signs with, on testnet OR mainnet, with no manual address.
#  Kept here only to document the confirmed testnet values (qwen2.5-omni):
#    provider 0xa48f01287233509FD694a22Bf840225062E67836
#    signer   0x83df4B8EbA7c0B3B740019b8c9a77ffF77D508cF
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 0G Storage — evidence layer (myTasks.md §C, Day 4). Public testnet endpoints, no key.
# Turbo indexer (recommended) per 0G docs; uploads are paid from COMPUTE_PRIVATE_KEY's wallet.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ZEROG_STORAGE_INDEXER_URL=https://indexer-storage-testnet-turbo.0g.ai
ZEROG_STORAGE_RPC_URL=https://evmrpc-testnet.0g.ai

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 0G Chain deploy — contracts (myTasks.md §D, Day 5).
# Deployer wallet for `hardhat.config.ts`. Same chain (16602) as Compute/Storage — you can
# reuse COMPUTE_PRIVATE_KEY here; just keep it faucet-funded for gas. Fund from the faucet above.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=0xREPLACE_ME
ENABLE_STORAGE=true

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional gas relayer (EIP-2771 "gasless" betting). Lets a spectator with ZERO native
# 0G sign a ForwardRequest while this relayer wallet submits it and pays gas. Entirely
# optional: leave RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY unset and the feature stays off (the UI falls back
# to the normal user-pays-gas path). See server/src/relayer.ts + contracts/Forwarder.sol.
#  - FORWARDER_ADDRESS:    the deployed Forwarder (printed by scripts/deploy.ts). MafiaMarket
#    and MockBetToken were deployed trusting THIS address — keep them in sync on every redeploy.
#  - RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY:  a SEPARATE funded wallet (NOT the host key — avoids nonce races with
#    match settle txs). Keep it topped up with testnet 0G; it pays everyone's gas.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
FORWARDER_ADDRESS=0xREPLACE_ME
RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY=0xREPLACE_ME

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend (Vite) — optional overrides; the code falls back to the in-repo defaults.
#  - VITE_FORWARDER_ADDRESS: only needed if the frontend reads the forwarder before the
#    server's /relay/info responds (the relay path discovers it from /relay/info otherwise).
#  - VITE_RELAYER_URL:       override the relay endpoint base (defaults to the page host / :8080).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_FORWARDER_ADDRESS=0x...
# VITE_RELAYER_URL=https://your-server.example.com

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional spoken-dialogue TTS — voices the players' lines (one voice per persona, tone-tagged).
# Entirely optional: leave ELEVENLABS_API_KEY unset and the feature stays OFF (the UI shows no
# voice control and never fetches audio; the typewriter still runs). The keys live ONLY here on
# the server — they are NEVER shipped to the browser. See server/src/tts.ts + voices.ts.
#  - ELEVENLABS_API_KEY:         a DIRECT ElevenLabs API key (gates the whole feature). May hold a
#                                comma/whitespace-separated LIST — synthesis rolls over to the next key
#                                when one runs out of credit (handy on the free tier, ~2-3 matches/key).
#  - ELEVENLABS_API_KEYS:        alias for the above (plural), takes precedence when both are set.
#  - ELEVENLABS_MODEL_ID:        `eleven_v3` understands the [tone] tags; `eleven_multilingual_v2`
#                                still speaks but ignores them. Defaults to eleven_v3.
#  - ELEVENLABS_DEFAULT_VOICE_ID: fallback voice for any persona not in the map.
#  - ELEVENLABS_VOICE_MAP:       optional JSON override of the name→voiceId map, e.g.
#                                {"Atlas":"<voiceId>","Vesper":"<voiceId>"} — merged over the defaults.
#  - NVIDIA_NIM_API_KEY:         optional (nvapi-… from build.nvidia.com, free). With it, a fast NIM
#                                model inserts the v3 tone tags from the line + game context; without
#                                it, a heuristic supplies the tags.
#  - TTS_LLM_MODEL:              the NIM tagger model (default meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct — keep it
#                                small; big models queue for minutes on the free catalog).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEYS=            # or several: key_one,key_two,key_three
# ELEVENLABS_MODEL_ID=eleven_v3
# ELEVENLABS_DEFAULT_VOICE_ID=
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_MAP=
# NVIDIA_NIM_API_KEY=
# TTS_LLM_MODEL=meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct
# Frontend (Vite) — only if the TTS server lives on a different host than the page:
# VITE_TTS_URL=https://your-server.example.com